MilkDropMetalKit

Third-party sources ported or adapted (handoff §3). Record each one here, with its licence, before the code lands.

Butterchurn — https://github.com/jberg/butterchurn — MIT
  Ported to Swift and Metal (structure, constants and formulas; no JavaScript or GLSL copied verbatim):
  - Sources/MilkMetal/AudioAnalyzer.swift: waveform undersampling, the equalised FFT, bass/mid/treb bands and their
    attack/release rates (audioProcessor.js, fft.js, audioLevels.js).
  - Sources/MilkMetal/PresetRuntime.swift and CustomRuntimes.swift: the per-frame/per-vertex/custom wave/custom
    shape equation flow, q and t variables, and the warp mesh (presetEquationRunner.js, renderer.js,
    customWaveform.js, customShape.js).
  - Sources/MilkMetal/Overlays.swift: built-in waveform modes 0–7, wave smoothing, motion vectors, borders and the
    darkened centre (basicWaveform.js, waveUtils.js, motionVectors.js, border.js, darkenCenter.js).
  - Sources/MilkMetal/Shaders.swift and MilkRenderer.swift: the default warp and composite (echo, gamma, hue
    corners, filters), the blur passes and their weights, sizes and ranges (warp.js, comp.js, blur*.js).
  - Sources/MilkMetal/NoiseTextures.swift: the noise textures (noise.js).
  - Sources/MilkShaders/Prelude.swift: the uniforms a preset shader sees and their values.

